{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1314128-about-forces-sphere","id":1314128,"title":"About Forces Sphere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-05-24T12:11:50-07:00","id":1314128,"title":"About Forces Sphere","content":"About the forces 5<br /> <br /> <br /> Hi I would like to talk about anexo Idea I have been brewing for some time and sharing it will let me see if it is mechanicaly possible.<br /> <br /> The forces sphere has a very weird problem that others dont follow, as the &quot;damages&quot; sphere it becomes quite paradoxical as you level it up to the point many people argues that it is nonsensical to so since mechanicaly you have much harder difficulties, paradox and even strict control of the end effect.<br /> <br /> Lets see here:<br /> <br /> Forces 3 - diff. 7<br /> <br /> * if done vulgar an effect will be 4+3(sphere level) <br /> <br /> Forces 4 - diff. 8<br /> <br /> * if done vulgar an effect will be 4+4(sphere level)<br /> <br /> Forces 5 - diff. 9<br /> <br /> * if done vulgar an effect will be 4+5(sphere level)<br /> <br /> <br /> Why would someone game wise invest on something that actually becomes absurdly impractical, if not unusable, as it becomes stronger?<br /> <br /> Ps.: Oh and by such logic Forces 6, the archsphere, has base diff. 10. Beautiful.<br /> <br /> Well I have some ideias that can be used:<br /> <br /> Bring Back the Golden Age, make it so that higher leves give stronger modifiers<br /> I) instead of static +1 damage it scalates after level 3 (so Forces 4 has +2 damage, Forces 5 +3, and so on.)<br /> <br /> II) make it so that each level after 3 makes it so that the successes multiplyer is bigger.<br /> <br /> Therefore, Forces 3 x 2, Forces 4 x 3, Forces 5 x 4, Forces 6 x 5<br /> <br /> So lets get some examples:<br /> <br /> Forces 3 with average 2 successes = (2x2)+1 = 5 damage.<br /> <br /> Forces 4 with average 2 successes = (2x3)+1 = 7 damage.<br /> <br /> Forces 5 with average 2 successes = (2x4)+1 = 9 damage.<br /> <br /> Forces 6 with average 2 successes = (2x5)+1 = 11 damage<br /> <br /> <br /> But that is crude math, what matters is the game. <br /> <br /> I find it quite annoying that Forces 4+ becomes so impractical since effects 4+ are always vulgar, and level 5 are obviously with witness. <br /> I think that any sphere level should be usable at any moment instead of ritual space only. So what if in the middle of a battlefield someone wants to creste a nuclear explosion? Wouldnt that be really reasonable for a Master of Forces? And what if the player or NPC just wants to overkill for the sake of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T12:49:32-07:00","id":1314142,"title":"","content":"The archmage(I think both of them) book made it very clear that everything an archmage does is most likely going to be a ritual and cost a ton of quintessence.<br /> <br /> The same can be said for most 4-5 spheres.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure a big use of forces 4-5 is simply &quot;Making storms&quot; and &quot;Blow up half the city&quot; and &quot;Nukes&quot;. Both of which are not something you will see in mage being done at 'a flick of the wrist'.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind these things, in M20, will require 10-15 successes.<br /> <br /> Use rituals.<br /> <br /> &quot;But I want to use powerful magic in combat&quot;<br /> <br /> Use forces 2-3 and with your high arete you will blow them away.<br /> <br /> &quot;So what if in the middle of a battlefield someone wants to creste a nuclear explosion? Wouldnt that be really reasonable for a Master of Forces? And what if the player or NPC just wants to overkill for the sake of it?&quot;<br /> <br /> Use a wonder or a charm with a forces 5 effect in it. Mage is a game of planning.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T11:23:14-07:00","id":1325015,"title":"","content":"Im sad no one else gave their opinions about this thread. The only one who did focused everything on a bit of the issue I pointed out. If somone wants to have their game with less magical stuff no problem at all, but the biggest problem here is not if someone can or not utilize sphere 4+ or plus for &quot;free&quot;, with I frankly see no problem at all. The real problem I am trying to show is that the game itself makes you NOT utilize your own character in a way that the very system say that should be possible (as in utilizing Forces beyond a starting character sheet build), and it is not resistrected to that but to other spheres as well, Forces is but all the most obnoxious example.<br /> <br /> Oh and since it became the central argument, whats the problem of somone having a nuke on their hand or anything like that? Even now you can do that even without forces 4+, you just need a ritual and thats that, the real thing is not about what a mage can do or not, but the consequences of such. What i argue here is that if one has such power why does the game works as if to prevent the player doing exactly that? And I know all about the fluff and so on, but mechanically the game punishes the player if he tries to get too much &quot;power&quot;, with annoyes me a lot since it looks l\u00e7ike the system tries to make you play &quot;the right way it was intended&quot;.<br /> <br /> Oh its just me or sometimes I get the feeling that there is a vibe to make mages less powerfull in front of other gamelines? I dont think its by the players, since mage is a game that each group plays in an unique way since it actually needs to be like that, and obviously WW is not about crossover, but in our system here everything pushes the setting in to a specific way of doing things.<br /> <br /> Well, thats it for my rant.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T11:48:15-07:00","id":1325025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>menos125</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1314128-about-forces-sphere?p=1325015#post1325015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real problem I am trying to show is that the game itself makes you NOT utilize your own character in a way that the very system say that should be possible (as in utilizing Forces beyond a starting character sheet build), and it is not resistrected to that but to other spheres as well, Forces is but all the most obnoxious example</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're not the only one who perceives that problem.<br /> <br /> My favored example it's the power to erase someone from existence at Prime 5. It's explicitly stated in fluff that this is a fearsome power, a feared attack spell...but really, it causes less damage than Prime 2/3 (for more risk of Paradox). It's useful if you just <i>happen </i>to have to kill someone that's trully immortal and regenerates from death (no body, no regen). Or if you <i>really </i>don't want to leave a body and can't be bothered to dispose it trough an additional, easier, spell. Otherwise it's always worse than cheaper solutions.<br /> <br /> I can see the idea of adding damage on the highest levels (it's not only what 1e did, but also what DA: Mage did). It has merit.<br /> <br /> Another option (in my opinion, more balanced) it's...not increasing the difficulty according to the Sphere Level. Have a fixed difficulty based on Vulgarity (say: 6, 7, 8. More if you want a harder Reality). This doesn't really add damage on the higher levels, but doesn't <i>penalize </i>them either...And thus they end being <i>better </i>because they can add things like &quot;Area of Effect&quot; (in the case of Forces), dematerialization, and other extreme goodies to the attack w/o somehow causing less damage. Arete takes care of sher power like it always did, and the higher levels are better because they add versatility like they're supposed to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-16-2019, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T14:24:20-07:00","id":1325066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1314128-about-forces-sphere?p=1325025#post1325025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option (in my opinion, more balanced) it's...not increasing the difficulty according to the Sphere Level. Have a fixed difficulty based on Vulgarity (say: 6, 7, 8. More if you want a harder Reality). This doesn't really add damage on the higher levels, but doesn't <i>penalize </i>them either...And thus they end being <i>better </i>because they can add things like &amp;quot;Area of Effect&amp;quot; (in the case of Forces), dematerialization, and other extreme goodies to the attack w/o somehow causing less damage. Arete takes care of sher power like it always did, and the higher levels are better because they add versatility like they're supposed to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I quite like that Idea since even If It has high dif you, by your instruments and other things, may lower the modifiers.<br /> <br /> Oh and what you think about those high lvl apheres, should they only be used on rituals or freely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T15:52:59-07:00","id":1325077,"title":"","content":"One thing you can do to make Forces 4-5 more effective is lower the number of successes required to do Effects at those levels. Forces is inherently <i>forceful</i> and it kind of makes sense that if you're going to make the bigger Effects higher Sphere level they should cost fewer successes compared to other Sphere effects of the same magnitude.<br /> <br /> But with the system overall, pretty much what Jihelu said. More powerful magic tends to require rituals and preparation--that is just the play style of Mage. It's not meant to nerf you, or make Mages weaker than the other gamelines. Mages are the most powerful playable WoD characters overall--trust me, they complain about it all the time in the general WoD forums here. You just have to commit more game time to the more powerful magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 07-16-2019, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T05:02:21-07:00","id":1325210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>menos125</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1314128-about-forces-sphere?p=1325066#post1325066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh and what you think about those high lvl apheres, should they only be used on rituals or freely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both. It's true that high level effects often require a ritual, but no book says nor implies that high level effects are always going to be casted trough ritual<br /> <br /> Ritual casting it's for &quot;powerful&quot; effects that have a trully epic scale. Like nuking a city or summoning an Archdemon. But that has little to do with Sphere level. I've never read anywhere that high Sphere level effects should be ritualized. On the contrary, I can name some effects that canonically use lvl 5 Spheres, yet are very easy.<br /> <br /> You can, canonically, make someone vanish from Reality with Prime 5 and 4 successes - hard, but for an Arete 5/6 Master it's far from impossible to do that in a turn, esp if the Master expends Willpower and lowers the difficulty to the minimum. It's statistically worse than killing someone with prime 3 because of the added difficulty, but it's not canonically intended to be a ritual (or at least the rules don't seem to imply that you need a ritual to do that)<br /> <br /> If you don't divide successes Time 5 classic &quot;time stop&quot; effect it's just 3 successes (relatively easy for a Master), if I remember the tables well.<br /> <br /> Sphere level adds more options that <i>should </i>require big rituals, but nowhere it's said that they <i>can't </i>be used to fast cast.<br /> <br /> The need of ritualization doesn't come from the Sphere Level but from the scale of the spell, which usualy implies ST judgement (as per the table of magical feats). It just happens that lvl 5 Spheres allow to cast far more godlike stuff than lvl 1 Spheres, and thus many &quot;common&quot; high level effects would, indeed, need a ritual. But correlation doesn't imply causation, and Sphere lvl shouldn't imply the need of rituals (neither the fluff nor the RAW point to this)<br /> <br /> If you want a system where this isn't the case you need to do more than increase the damage. 1e Mage hadn't ritual rules <i>per se</i>, it hadn't a &quot;magical feats table&quot; ranging from 1 to 20 successes. Characters were theoretically capable of releasing any effect within a turn or so because of how the tables were built and intended to be used (altrough you would need Forces 6 to nuke a city under that system)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-17-2019, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T21:38:19-07:00","id":1325487,"title":"","content":"I don't know that I even agree with the premise that &quot;leveling up&quot; Forces should scale up your combat magic effectiveness? I don't think Mage has ever really been that type of game. Sphere dots primarily increase the *breadth* of your capabilities. But throwing a lightning bolt is still a Forces 3 / Prime 2 effect even if you have Forces 5 &amp; Prime 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T05:48:45-07:00","id":1325570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1314128-about-forces-sphere?p=1325487#post1325487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know that I even agree with the premise that &quot;leveling up&quot; Forces should scale up your combat magic effectiveness? I don't think Mage has ever really been that type of game. Sphere dots primarily increase the *breadth* of your capabilities. But throwing a lightning bolt is still a Forces 3 / Prime 2 effect even if you have Forces 5 &amp; Prime 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I understand this well, t<i>he</i> problem it's not that throwing a ligthining bolt it's effective, but that higger level combat options are <i>penalized</i>. And nowhere in mage it's said that this should be the case.<br /> <br /> Suddenly the Prime 2/Forces 2 effect to increase the cinetic energy of an attack becomes the most damaging form of magick. Only superseeded in specific circumstances, like when you need a spell to pierce armor or have some other kind of &quot;special effect&quot;.<br /> <br /> Throwing a <i>lightning bolt</i> (like you say) it's useless unless you either have no combat Skills (hence argumenting an attack becomes less effective) or you're in a situation where electricity it's the best form of damage for some reason...And high level combat magicks like Prime 5 &quot;critical failure to exist&quot; become useless except in the rarest of circumnstances (i.e, facing an Immortal).<br /> <br /> Something that, btw, nothing in the fluff indicates. No book shows mages using Forces 2/Prime 2 as the ULTIMATE attack spell, nor low level magick being the most used by Archmages in combat. There's also some clear disagreement among the Authors about that, because while the general rules say it's less efficient to use high level magick, many books have combat Rotes causing more damage at those levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T10:31:46-07:00","id":1325646,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer. I did forget as to explain that thought of spheres at high level becoming &quot;ritual only&quot;. I had that premise becausa mathematichaly they have such exhagerated dif modifiers that a level 5 effect becomes almost Impossible outside the ritual field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T10:39:40-07:00","id":1325648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1314128-about-forces-sphere?p=1325487#post1325487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know that I even agree with the premise that &amp;quot;leveling up&amp;quot; Forces should scale up your combat magic effectiveness? I don't think Mage has ever really been that type of game. Sphere dots primarily increase the *breadth* of your capabilities. But throwing a lightning bolt is still a Forces 3 / Prime 2 effect even if you have Forces 5 &amp; Prime 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well thats a central things on mage, its Impossible to play without houserules. So no one can trully say &quot;This is not how it should be played&quot;. You can be political, social, high magical, street magic or anything else as much as you want, the issue here is that the game mechanichs are, by a lot, not.double checked by devs, and such weird stances keep popping up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T12:51:40-07:00","id":1325705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>menos125</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1314128-about-forces-sphere?p=1325648#post1325648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well thats a central things on mage, its Impossible to play without houserules. So no one can trully say &quot;This is not how it should be played&quot;. You can be political, social, high magical, street magic or anything else as much as you want, the issue here is that the game mechanichs are, by a lot, not.double checked by devs, and such weird stances keep popping up.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does it being impossible to play without houserules follow from what Blackwell said?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T20:11:34-07:00","id":1325835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1314128-about-forces-sphere?p=1325705#post1325705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does it being impossible to play without houserules follow from what Blackwell said?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like i answered something thinking of another thing hahahahah","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T20:33:48-07:00","id":1325841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>menos125</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1314128-about-forces-sphere?p=1325835#post1325835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looks like i answered something thinking of another thing hahahahah</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I thought your response was reasonable. In my post there were definitely some whiffs (not intentional) of &quot;you're doing it wrong&quot; so... fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}